"program_narrative": "Program AUDPROC is a called audit-trail subroutine that receives one audit request LS-AUDIT-REQUEST (PROCEDURE DIVISION USING) and appends it as a record to the sequential audit file AUDIT-FILE (DD AUDFILE). It captures the current timestamp, opens the file in EXTEND (append) mode, builds AUDIT-RECORD from the request (system information, audit type, action, status, portfolio/account key, before and after images, message) and writes it. If the file cannot be opened it displays an error, returns code 8, closes the file and returns to the caller immediately; if the write fails it displays an error and returns 8, otherwise it returns 0. The file is closed before every return. The way the system-information group is moved over the record header overwrites the captured timestamp and is flagged for review.",
